/*
shutdownAction
--------------

Tells the IDE what to do with the container when its tool window closes or the
backend shuts down.

  • none          – Leave the container running.
  • stopContainer – Stop just this container (default for images/Dockerfiles).
  • stopCompose   – Shut down the entire Docker Compose stack (default for
                    Compose).

Choose **none** if you want the container to stay alive after the IDE
disconnects—for example:

  • **Long-running jobs** (model training, large data processing).
  • **Background services** (web servers, databases) you still need.
  • **Quicker return**—re-connecting is faster than a full restart.
*/

{
  "name": "1_10-spec_shutdownAction",
  "image": "ubuntu:latest",
  "shutdownAction": "none"
}
